course: dictionary
lesson: 1495
title: Hollow words: cavity
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A cavity is a hollow space inside something solid. The clue is in the word hollow, which means empty on the inside. «A hole in a tooth caused by decay is called a cavity.» Here the empty hole in the tooth is the cavity, and decay is what made it.
explain: Context tells you which kind of cavity is meant. At the dentist, a cavity is a hole that needs a filling. «Bacteria in plaque feed on sugar and make acid» explains how the hole starts. In science, cavity can mean any hollow space, such as the chest cavity in the body.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Put "hollow space" in place of cavity: «A bad hollow space in a tooth can cause toothache» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Cavity is a noun. One is a cavity, and more than one is cavities.
fact: «Cavity» means a hollow space inside something solid.
fact: «Cavity» can mean a small hole in a tooth caused by decay.
fact: A body cavity is a space inside the body, such as the chest or the mouth.
fact: Useful phrases: «fill a cavity», «cavity wall», «nasal cavity».
exercise: «A hole in a tooth caused by decay is called a cavity.» What is a cavity in this sentence? | *A hole in a tooth caused by decay | A type of toothbrush | A tooth that has been brushed clean | A kind of sugar
exercise: «The dentist has to clean out the hole and fill it before it reaches the nerve.» What is the dentist filling? | The sugar on the plate | The bones of the face | *The cavity in the tooth | The toothbrush
exercise: «The chest cavity holds the heart and lungs.» What does the chest cavity hold? | The teeth and gums | *The heart and lungs | The sugar and the acid | The school bags
test: Which word means a hollow space inside something solid? | *Cavity | Filling | Plaque | Enamel
test: Germs eat sugar left on teeth and make a substance that causes holes called cavities. What is it? | *Acid | Air | Salt | Water
exam: Which option best describes a body cavity? | *A hollow space inside the body, such as the chest | A bad smell from the mouth | A loud noise made by teeth | A kind of food eaten at lunch
